# Information about `TIFFFlush`

## Function Signature

```c

extern int TIFFFlush(TIFF* tif);
```

## Source Code

```c
int TIFFFlush(TIFF* tif) {
  if (tif->tif_mode == O_RDONLY)
    return 1;

  if (!TIFFFlushData(tif))
    return (0);

  /* In update (r+) mode we try to detect the case where
     only the strip/tile map has been altered, and we try to
     rewrite only that portion of the directory without
     making any other changes */

  if ((tif->tif_flags & TIFF_DIRTYSTRIP) && !(tif->tif_flags & TIFF_DIRTYDIRECT) && tif->tif_mode == O_RDWR) {
    if (TIFFForceStrileArrayWriting(tif))
      return 1;
  }

  if ((tif->tif_flags & (TIFF_DIRTYDIRECT | TIFF_DIRTYSTRIP)) && !TIFFRewriteDirectory(tif))
    return (0);

  return (1);
}
```

2026-08-28 19:19:45
Response for query 94 after 0.99s:
`TIFFFlush` writes pending image data and, if needed, updates the directory. Use it after writing/updating a TIFF to force buffered data out. In `O_RDONLY` it’s a no-op success. In `O_RDWR`, it may rewrite only strip/tile maps or the full directory; failures return 0.
