Decodes a packed 32-bit LogLuv pixel into XYZ tristimulus values. Use it with a `uint32_t` LogLuv sample and a 3-float output array. If decoded luminance `L<=0`, it returns `{0,0,0}`; otherwise it computes XYZ from luminance and chromaticity.
