# Information about `uv_decode`

## Function Signature

```c

extern int uv_decode(double*, double*, int);
```

## Source Code

```c
int uv_decode(double *up, double *vp, int c) /* decode (u',v') index */
{
  int upper, lower;
  register int ui, vi;

  if (c < 0 || c >= UV_NDIVS)
    return (-1);
  lower = 0; /* binary search */
  upper = UV_NVS;
  while (upper - lower > 1) {
    vi = (lower + upper) >> 1;
    ui = c - uv_row[vi].ncum;
    if (ui > 0)
      lower = vi;
    else if (ui < 0)
      upper = vi;
    else {
      lower = vi;
      break;
    }
  }
  vi = lower;
  ui = c - uv_row[vi].ncum;
  *up = uv_row[vi].ustart + (ui + .5) * UV_SQSIZ;
  *vp = UV_VSTART + (vi + .5) * UV_SQSIZ;
  return (0);
}
```

2026-08-28 19:21:48
Response for query 252 after 0.98s:
Decodes a UV index `c` into the center coordinates `(u',v')`. Use with valid `0 <= c < UV_NDIVS`; on success it writes `*up,*vp` and returns `0`, otherwise returns `-1`. It binary-searches `uv_row` to map the index.
