# Information about `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8`

## Function Signature

```c

extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8(uint64_t* lp, tmsize_t n);
```

## Source Code

```c
void TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8(register uint64_t *lp, tmsize_t n) {
  register unsigned char *cp;
  register unsigned char t;
  assert(sizeof(uint64_t) == 8);
  /* XXX unroll loop some */
  while (n-- > 0) {
    cp = (unsigned char *)lp;
    t = cp[7];
    cp[7] = cp[0];
    cp[0] = t;
    t = cp[6];
    cp[6] = cp[1];
    cp[1] = t;
    t = cp[5];
    cp[5] = cp[2];
    cp[2] = t;
    t = cp[4];
    cp[4] = cp[3];
    cp[3] = t;
    lp++;
  }
}
```

2026-08-28 19:22:34
Response for query 314 after 0.81s:
Swaps byte order of an array of 64-bit integers in place. Use it on `n` `uint64_t` values when TIFF data endianness differs. It always processes all `n` elements; `n==0` does nothing.
