2. `TIFFTileSize64`
​ `TIFFTileSize64` returns the size in bytes of one tile as a `uint64_t`. It’s a convenience wrapper around `TIFFVTileSize64(tif, tif->tif_dir.td_tilelength)`, so use it on a valid `TIFF*` after tile parameters are set. It just computes and returns the tile size.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern uint64_t TIFFTileSize64(TIFF* tif);
​ ```
3. `TIFFVStripSize64`
​ Returns the byte size of a strip for `nrows` rows. Use `nrows==(uint32_t)-1` to mean full image height. For packed, non-upsampled YCbCr contiguous data it accounts for subsampling/round-up; invalid `SamplesPerPixel` returns 0 and logs an error.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern uint64_t TIFFVStripSize64(TIFF* tif, uint32_t nrows);
​ ```
4. `TIFFVTileSize64`
​ Computes the byte size of a tile for `nrows` rows. Use it after tile geometry is set; returns 0 if tilewidth/length/depth are unset. Special-cases packed YCbCr contig data with subsampling, rounding up for partial blocks.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern uint64_t TIFFVTileSize64(TIFF* tif, uint32_t nrows);
​ ```
5. `TIFFStripSize64`
​ `TIFFStripSize64` returns the byte size of a strip for the current TIFF, using `RowsPerStrip` capped to `ImageLength`. Use it after `TIFF*` is initialized to size/read/write strip buffers. If `RowsPerStrip > ImageLength`, it uses `ImageLength`; result comes from `TIFFVStripSize64`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern uint64_t TIFFStripSize64(TIFF* tif);
​ ```
6. `TIFFScanlineSize64`
​ `TIFFScanlineSize64` returns the byte size of one image row, using 64-bit math to avoid overflow on very large images. Use it after TIFF tags are set/read. It handles contig YCbCr subsampling specially; invalid tag values may trigger an error and return 0.
