Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libtiff using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `TIFFUnsetField`
​ `TIFFUnsetField` clears a TIFF tag from the directory. Use it with a TIFF handle and tag ID. Returns 0 if the tag isn’t known; otherwise it clears the standard field bit, or removes/frees a custom tag value and shifts the custom list.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern int TIFFUnsetField(TIFF*, uint32_t);
​ ```
2. `TIFFMergeFieldInfo`
​ Adds a compatibility field-array to a TIFF handle. Call it with a valid `TIFF*` and an array of `TIFFFieldInfo` to register extra/custom tags. Returns `-1` on allocation failure; otherwise it appends the merged field set.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern int TIFFMergeFieldInfo(TIFF*, const TIFFFieldInfo[], uint32_t);
​ ```
3. `TIFFCreateCustomDirectory`
​ Creates a new “custom” TIFF directory: resets to default state, then installs the app’s field definitions via `_TIFFSetupFields()`. Use it before writing/using a nonstandard directory. It clears offsets/row/strip state and always returns 0.
Yes, this crash is caused by misuse of the API. Do not pass NULL as the infoarray argument. Invoke TIFFCreateCustomDirectory(tif, infoarray) only with a valid, fully initialized TIFFFieldArray* that describes the custom directory fields, including a valid fields pointer and correct count. If no custom field definitions are needed, avoid calling this API and use standard directory creation APIs instead. Also validate pointers before calling and handle a failure return defensively.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern int TIFFCreateCustomDirectory(TIFF*, const TIFFFieldArray*);
​ ```
4. `TIFFFreeDirectory`
​ `TIFFFreeDirectory` frees/reset the current `TIFF` directory’s allocated field data and custom tag values. Use it to clean up a directory before reusing/destroying the `TIFF`; it clears field bits, frees owned buffers, and resets allocation state.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFFreeDirectory(TIFF*);
​ ```
5. `TIFFGetTagListEntry`
​ Returns the tag ID at `tag_index` from `tif->tif_dir.td_customValues`. Use it to iterate custom tags by index. If `tag_index` is <0 or >= `td_customValueCount`, it returns `(uint32_t)-1`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern uint32_t TIFFGetTagListEntry(TIFF *, int tag_index);
​ ```
6. `TIFFGetFieldDefaulted`
​ `TIFFGetFieldDefaulted` is a varargs wrapper for `TIFFVGetFieldDefaulted`. Use it to read a tag from `tif`, getting the tag’s stored value or a default if the tag isn’t set. It returns the underlying success status from `TIFFVGetFieldDefaulted`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern int TIFFGetFieldDefaulted(TIFF* tif, uint32_t tag, ...);
​ ```

## Related Data Types

```c
struct _TIFFFieldArray {
 TIFFFieldArrayType type; /* array type, will be used to determine if IFD is image and such */
 uint32_t allocated_size; /* 0 if array is constant, other if modified by future definition extension support */
 uint32_t count; /* number of elements in fields array */
 TIFFField* fields; /* actual field info */
};

struct _TIFFField {
 uint32_t field_tag; /* field's tag */
 short field_readcount; /* read count/TIFF_VARIABLE/TIFF_SPP */
 short field_writecount; /* write count/TIFF_VARIABLE */
 TIFFDataType field_type; /* type of associated data */
 uint32_t reserved; /* reserved for future extension */
 TIFFSetGetFieldType set_field_type; /* type to be passed to TIFFSetField */
 TIFFSetGetFieldType get_field_type; /* type to be passed to TIFFGetField */
 unsigned short field_bit; /* bit in fieldsset bit vector */
 unsigned char field_oktochange; /* if true, can change while writing */
 unsigned char field_passcount; /* if true, pass dir count on set */
 char* field_name; /* ASCII name */
 TIFFFieldArray* field_subfields; /* if field points to child ifds, child ifd field definition array */
};

struct tiff {
 char* tif_name; /* name of open file */
 int tif_fd; /* open file descriptor */
 int tif_mode; /* open mode (O_*) */
 uint32_t tif_flags;
#define TIFF_FILLORDER 0x00003U /* natural bit fill order for machine */
#define TIFF_DIRTYHEADER 0x00004U /* header must be written on close */
#define TIFF_DIRTYDIRECT 0x00008U /* current directory must be written */
#define TIFF_BUFFERSETUP 0x00010U /* data buffers setup */
#define TIFF_CODERSETUP 0x00020U /* encoder/decoder setup done */
#define TIFF_BEENWRITING 0x00040U /* written 1+ scanlines to file */
#define TIFF_SWAB 0x00080U /* byte swap file information */
#define TIFF_NOBITREV 0x00100U /* inhibit bit reversal logic */
#define TIFF_MYBUFFER 0x00200U /* my raw data buffer; free on close */
#define TIFF_ISTILED 0x00400U /* file is tile, not strip- based */
#define TIFF_MAPPED 0x00800U /* file is mapped into memory */
#define TIFF_POSTENCODE 0x01000U /* need call to postencode routine */
#define TIFF_INSUBIFD 0x02000U /* currently writing a subifd */
#define TIFF_UPSAMPLED 0x04000U /* library is doing data up-sampling */
#define TIFF_STRIPCHOP 0x08000U /* enable strip chopping support */
#define TIFF_HEADERONLY 0x10000U /* read header only, do not process the first directory */
#define TIFF_NOREADRAW 0x20000U /* skip reading of raw uncompressed image data */
#define TIFF_INCUSTOMIFD 0x40000U /* currently writing a custom IFD */
#define TIFF_BIGTIFF 0x80000U /* read/write bigtiff */
#define TIFF_BUF4WRITE 0x100000U /* rawcc bytes are for writing */
#define TIFF_DIRTYSTRIP 0x200000U /* stripoffsets/stripbytecount dirty*/
#define TIFF_PERSAMPLE 0x400000U /* get/set per sample tags as arrays */
#define TIFF_BUFFERMMAP 0x800000U /* read buffer (tif_rawdata) points into mmap() memory */
#define TIFF_DEFERSTRILELOAD 0x1000000U /* defer strip/tile offset/bytecount array loading. */
#define TIFF_LAZYSTRILELOAD 0x2000000U /* lazy/ondemand loading of strip/tile offset/bytecount values. Only used if TIFF_DEFERSTRILELOAD is set and in read-only mode */
#define TIFF_CHOPPEDUPARRAYS 0x4000000U /* set when allocChoppedUpStripArrays() has modified strip array */
 uint64_t tif_diroff; /* file offset of current directory */
