Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libtiff using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `TIFFSwabArrayOfFloat`
​ `TIFFSwabArrayOfFloat` byte-swaps `n` 4-byte floats in place. Use it on float arrays when TIFF data endianness differs from the host. It assumes `sizeof(float)==4`; with `n<=0` it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfFloat(float* fp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
2. `TIFFSwabLong`
​ `TIFFSwabLong` byte-swaps one 32-bit `uint32_t` in place. Use it on a valid pointer to a 4-byte value when converting between endiannesses. It simply reverses the 4 bytes; no return value, no checks beyond the size assert.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabLong(uint32_t*);
​ ```
3. `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong`
​ `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong` byte-swaps an array of 32-bit unsigned integers in place. Use it when TIFF data endianness differs from the host. It processes `n` elements, swapping each `uint32_t`; if `n<=0`, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfLong(uint32_t* lp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
4. `TIFFSwabArrayOfTriples`
​ Swaps byte order in-place for an array of 3-byte records (“triples”): each item’s 1st and 3rd bytes are exchanged, middle byte unchanged. Use on `tp` with `n` triples. If `n<=0`, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfTriples(uint8_t* tp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
5. `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8`
​ Swaps byte order of an array of 64-bit integers in place. Use it on `n` `uint64_t` values when TIFF data endianness differs. It always processes all `n` elements; `n==0` does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8(uint64_t* lp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
6. `TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble`
​ Swaps byte order of an array of `double` in place. Use it on `n` 8-byte doubles when TIFF data endianness differs from the host. It asserts `sizeof(double)==8`; `n==0` does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble(double* dp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```

