2. `TIFFGetClientInfo`
​ `TIFFGetClientInfo` looks up a client-info entry by `name` in a `TIFF*` and returns its stored `void*` data. Use it after client info has been attached to that TIFF handle. If no matching name exists, it returns `NULL`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void *TIFFGetClientInfo(TIFF *, const char *);
​ ```
3. `TIFFMergeFieldInfo`
​ Adds a compatibility field-array to a TIFF handle. Call it with a valid `TIFF*` and an array of `TIFFFieldInfo` to register extra/custom tags. Returns `-1` on allocation failure; otherwise it appends the merged field set.
