5. `TIFFClientOpen`
​ `TIFFClientOpen` creates a TIFF handle using caller-supplied I/O callbacks, so libtiff can read/write from custom sources (memory, network, etc.). Pass the client data and valid read/write/seek/close/size/map/unmap funcs. It returns a `TIFF*` on success, `NULL` on failure.
