2. `TIFFWriteCustomDirectory`
​ `TIFFWriteCustomDirectory` is a thin wrapper around `TIFFWriteDirectorySec`. It writes the current TIFF directory as a “custom” directory, storing the new directory offset in `*pdiroff`. Use it with a valid `TIFF*` and non-NULL `uint64_t*`. It returns the underlying write status.
