## Target API Functions

1. `TIFFSwabArrayOfShort`
​ `TIFFSwabArrayOfShort` byte-swaps an array of 16-bit values in place. Use it on `wp` with `n` elements when TIFF data endianness differs from host order. It loops over each `uint16_t`; `n<=0` does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfShort(uint16_t* wp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
2. `TIFFSwabShort`
​ `TIFFSwabShort` byte-swaps a 16-bit `uint16_t` in place. Pass a valid pointer to one short; it swaps the two bytes regardless of host endianness. It assumes `sizeof(uint16_t)==2` and uses `assert` for that.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabShort(uint16_t*);
​ ```
3. `TIFFSwabLong8`
​ `TIFFSwabLong8` byte-swaps a 64-bit unsigned integer in place, converting between little- and big-endian order. Pass a valid `uint64_t*`; it always swaps all 8 bytes and assumes `sizeof(uint64_t)==8`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabLong8(uint64_t*);
​ ```
4. `TIFFSwabDouble`
​ `TIFFSwabDouble` byte-swaps an 8-byte `double` in place. Use it on a valid `double*` when converting between opposite-endian TIFF data and host order. It simply reverses the 8 bytes; `assert` expects `sizeof(double)==8`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabDouble(double*);
​ ```
5. `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8`
​ Swaps byte order of an array of 64-bit integers in place. Use it on `n` `uint64_t` values when TIFF data endianness differs. It always processes all `n` elements; `n==0` does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8(uint64_t* lp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
6. `TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble`
​ Swaps byte order of an array of `double` in place. Use it on `n` 8-byte doubles when TIFF data endianness differs from the host. It asserts `sizeof(double)==8`; `n==0` does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble(double* dp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```

