Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libtiff using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `TIFFErrorExt`
​ `TIFFErrorExt` reports a TIFF error with an extra `thandle_t` context. Call it with `fd`, optional `module`, and printf-style `fmt/...`. It invokes the installed error handlers if present; if none are set, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFErrorExt(thandle_t, const char*, const char*, ...) TIFF_ATTRIBUTE((__format__(__printf__, 3, 4)));
​ ```
2. `TIFFWarningExt`
​ `TIFFWarningExt` emits a formatted TIFF warning. Call it with a client handle, module name, and printf-style format. It forwards the warning to the installed warning handler(s); if none are set, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFWarningExt(thandle_t, const char*, const char*, ...) TIFF_ATTRIBUTE((__format__(__printf__, 3, 4)));
​ ```
3. `TIFFSetWarningHandler`
​ `TIFFSetWarningHandler` sets libtiff’s global warning callback and returns the previous one. Use it to install your own warning handler or restore an old one. Passing `NULL` disables warning reporting via the handler.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFFErrorHandler TIFFSetWarningHandler(TIFFErrorHandler);
​ ```
4. `TIFFSetErrorHandlerExt`
​ `TIFFSetErrorHandlerExt` sets the global extended TIFF error callback and returns the previous one. Use it to install or replace a handler; pass `NULL` to disable it. It affects later TIFF errors only, not past ones.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFFErrorHandlerExt TIFFSetErrorHandlerExt(TIFFErrorHandlerExt);
​ ```
5. `TIFFSetWarningHandlerExt`
​ `TIFFSetWarningHandlerExt` sets libtiff’s extended warning callback and returns the previous one. Use it to install or replace a `TIFFErrorHandlerExt`; pass `NULL` to disable warnings. It has no other logic beyond swapping the global handler.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFFErrorHandlerExt TIFFSetWarningHandlerExt(TIFFErrorHandlerExt);
​ ```
6. `TIFFSetErrorHandler`
​ `TIFFSetErrorHandler` sets libtiff’s global error-reporting callback and returns the previous handler. Use it to install your own `TIFFErrorHandler`; pass `NULL` to disable handling. It affects subsequent TIFF errors globally.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFFErrorHandler TIFFSetErrorHandler(TIFFErrorHandler);
​ ```

